  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Peace in Ethiopia through Community Policing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed programme is part of the aspiration of the Ministry of Peace of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia (FDRE) and Interpeace to build trust between the country&#x2019;s institutions and its citizens. In the case of the police, the Ministry of Peace has identified its approach to rebuilding a police force which can be trusted in the Police Doctrine, published in 2020. This particular project is for a three-month engagement in two Woreda&apos;s to develop data-based problem-solving approaches to begin the process of building trust between the police and the communities and, thus, put in place the initial building blocks for a successful community policing model, which can be replicated across the country.</narrative>
  </description>
